  "gaps": [
    "Major credit totals conflict: the course list is headed 'Requirements (54 credit hours)' (18 courses x 3 = 54), but the summary shows '57 Major Requirements Credits'. The capture does not explain the 3-credit difference.",
    "STS 280 and STS 290 (3 credits total) are required only for international students. The capture does not say whether these credits count toward the 57 major credits, toward electives, or are added for domestic students.",
    "The capture requires the Kirkpatrick Signature Series in addition to the major requirements, but it does not list the courses or credits, or say which bucket they count toward.",
    "The capture does not list specific general education courses or clusters, only the 37-credit total.",
    "BSCL 320 and BSCL 410 are named as prerequisites (for BSCL 335, 435, 440 and 445) but are not listed among the program requirements.",
    "Prerequisites outside the major list (BA 252, MA 215, MA 102 or MA 120, EN 101 and EN 102) are not identified as part of the general education or elective blocks.",
    "BSCL 336 (3 credits) is an optional program elective, not a requirement, so it is excluded. The capture does not say whether it counts toward the 33 elective credits.",
    "The capture does not state residency, institutional-credit, upper-division or minimum grade requirements.",
    "The capture does not state the catalog year; it says current students should consult BRUIN 'Academic Progress' for curriculum requirements."
